1
00:00:00,523 --> 00:00:02,943
Leonard? Leonard?

2
00:00:04,152 --> 00:00:06,492
(Leonard(following Sheldon into living room):)- What?
- I was analyzing our lie...

3
00:00:06,654 --> 00:00:09,744
(Sheldon:)...and I believe we're in danger
of Penny seeing through the ruse.

4
00:00:10,158 --> 00:00:12,118
- How?
- Simple.

5
00:00:12,285 --> 00:00:17,455
If she were to log on to www.
socalphysicsgroup.org/activities/other...

6
00:00:17,624 --> 00:00:21,164
...click on upcoming events, scroll to
seminars, download the PDF schedule...

7
00:00:21,336 --> 00:00:24,126
(Sheldon:)...and look for the seminar
on molecular positronium, then...

8
00:00:24,297 --> 00:00:28,007
...bippity boppity boo,
our pants are metaphorically on fire.

9
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:36,060
(Sheldon:)Well, sir, my trousers
will not be igniting today.

10
00:00:38,561 --> 00:00:39,771
Penny?

11
00:00:39,938 --> 00:00:41,148
Penny?

12
00:00:41,314 --> 00:00:42,944
Penny?

13
00:00:43,483 --> 00:00:44,653
(Sheldon:)Good morning.

14
00:00:44,818 --> 00:00:47,528
- Do you have any idea what time it is?
- Of course I do.

15
00:00:47,695 --> 00:00:51,495
(Sheldon:)My watch is linked to the atomic clock
in Boulder, Colorado.

16
00:00:51,658 --> 00:00:54,118
It's accurate to one-tenth of a second.

17
00:00:54,285 --> 00:00:56,495
(Sheldon:)As I'm saying this
it occurs to me once again...

18
00:00:56,663 --> 00:00:59,203
(Sheldon:)...your question may
have been rhetorical.

19
00:00:59,666 --> 00:01:01,026
(Penny:)What do you want?

